<style>
/* Motor styling */
.rm-motor-wrap {
  max-width: 1300px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 14px 22px;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  color: #1b1b1b;
}

.rm-motor-card {
  border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.12);
  border-radius: 14px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(0,0,0,.08);
  margin: 14px 0;
  background: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-1b {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #bc9923;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-1dab {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #bc9923;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-2b {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #1d3748;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-2dab {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #1d3748;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-4hd {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #5d3324;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-6 {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #2c5f2d;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-1b h3,
.rm-motor-head-1dab h3,
.rm-motor-head-2b h3,
.rm-motor-head-2dab h3,
.rm-motor-head-4hd h3,
.rm-motor-head-6 h3 {
  margin: 0;
  margin-bottom: 5px;
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: .2px;
}

.rm-motor-sub {
  margin: 6px 0 0;
  font-size: 13px;
  opacity: .9;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.rm-motor-body {
  padding: 14px 16px 16px;
}

.rm-motor-body p {
  margin: 0 0 10px;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.rm-motor-feats {
  margin: 10px 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 8px 14px;
}

.rm-motor-feats li {
  margin: 0;
  padding-left: 22px;
  position: relative;
  line-height: 1.35;
}

.rm-motor-feats li:before {
  content: "✓";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 0;
  color: #0a7a2f;
  font-weight: 900;
}

.rm-motor-note {
  margin-top: 10px;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  background: rgba(129,15,18,.08);
  border: 1px solid rgba(129,15,18,.18);
  color: #2a2a2a;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.35;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .rm-motor-feats {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
</style>

{% if DAB %}
<!-- Main Content Section -->
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 20px; gap: 20px; max-width: 100%;">
  <!-- Image Section -->
<div style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</div>
<!-- Description Section -->
<div style="flex: 2; min-width: 300px; padding: 10px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: #333;">{{ product.title }}</h2>
<p>
    The RetroSound Traffic is the premier radio solution for Modern Classics, designed specifically for European vehicles
    with factory Single DIN openings. Inspired by the functional OEM styling of the late-1980s through the early-2000s,
    the Traffic provides a period-correct look for BMW, Porsche, and Mercedes-Benz interiors.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unlike standard aftermarket decks that look out of place, the Traffic features a low-profile face, subtle
    push-buttons, and a variable-color display to match your factory dash lighting perfectly. Its understated design
    makes it an ideal upgrade for enthusiasts looking to preserve the authentic aesthetic of their dashboard while
    adding modern audio capability like Bluetooth&reg; connectivity and USB inputs.
  </p>
  <p>
    Part of the RetroSound DIN Solutions lineup, the Traffic is engineered for easy installation without costly dash
    modifications. The <a href="https://www.retromanufacturing.com/pages/retrosound-radio-motors">modular radio motor
    system</a> allows you to choose the feature set that best fits your driving style, ranging from essential classic car
    stereo functionality to <a href="https://www.retromanufacturing.com/pages/retrosound-radio-control-app-information">advanced
    app-based control</a> on select radio motor configurations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Whether restoring a daily driver or completing a high-end Modern Classic build, the RetroSound Traffic Radio
    delivers the factory look of a vintage European radio with the performance and flexibility of a modern retro-style
    stereo.
  </p>

<!-- Key Features Box -->
